  "worked_solution": "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧,$\" while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨.$\"\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts: \n\n- **Part 1:** $x$ is negative and irrational. This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{x\\,\\text{is negative}}_{⏟}}_{N}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{x\\,\\text{is irrational}}_{⏟}}_{W},\n$$\n\nthat is, $N∧W.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $x$ is positive and less than $5.$ This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{x\\text{ is positive }}_{⏟}}_{P}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{x\\text{ is less than }5}_{⏟}}_{U},\n$$\n\nthat is, $P∧U.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n{{x\\,\\text{is negative and irrational}}_{⏟}}_{N∧W}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{x\\text{ is positive and less than }5}_{⏟}}_{P∧U},\n$$\n\nthat is, $(N∧W)∨(P∧U).$",
